 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Custom YOLOv8 Model Training for Self-Driving AR HUD\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook guides you through training a custom YOLOv8 model for the browser-based AR HUD.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Prerequisites\n",
    "1. Ensure you have downloaded a dataset (e.g., from Roboflow Universe) that contains bounding box annotations in **YOLOv8 format**.\n",
    "2. Extract the dataset into a folder named `Dataset` in the same directory as this notebook.\n",
    "3. The `Dataset` folder should contain a `data.yaml` file (which specifies the classes and paths to train/val images).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Expected Classes\n",
    "Your dataset should ideally contain the following classes for the AR HUD to function as requested:\n",
    "`cars`, `pedestrians`, `traffic signs` (specifically Stop, Go, Speed Limit), `cycles`, `bikes`, `animals`, `zebra crossing`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install ultralytics tensorflowjs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Train the Model\n",
    "We use `yolov8n.pt` (Nano) as the starting point to ensure high FPS (target: 28+ FPS) in the browser."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load a pre-trained YOLOv8 Nano model (recommended for web/real-time)\n",
    "model = YOLO('yolov8n.pt')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure the dataset yaml exists\n",
    "dataset_yaml = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'Dataset', 'data.yaml')\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(dataset_yaml):\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: Cannot find {dataset_yaml}. Please make sure your dataset is placed correctly.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Train the model\n",
    "    # Adjust 'epochs' depending on your dataset size and hardware (50-100 is usually a good start).\n",
    "    # Adjust 'imgsz' to 640, which is standard for YOLO, but lower values (e.g., 416 or 320) will improve FPS.\n",
    "    results = model.train(data=dataset_yaml, epochs=50, imgsz=640, device='cuda' if os.path.exists('/usr/bin/nvidia-smi') else 'cpu')\n",
    "    print(\"Training Complete!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Validate the Model\n",
    "Check the performance on the validation set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "metrics = model.val()\n",
    "print(metrics.box.map) # Check Mean Average Precision"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Export to TensorFlow.js\n",
    "This is the most critical step for the Web application. We need to export the trained `.pt` weights into the `tfjs` format."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Export the best model to TFJS format\n",
    "best_model_path = os.path.join('runs', 'detect', 'train', 'weights', 'best.pt')\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(best_model_path):\n",
    "    best_model = YOLO(best_model_path)\n",
    "    # The export command will generate a folder with 'model.json' and '.bin' weight files.\n",
    "    best_model.export(format='tfjs')\n",
    "    print(\"Export complete! Check the runs/detect/train/weights/best_web_model/ folder.\")\n",
    "    print(\"You should copy the generated TFJS folder into your SelfDriving-AR-HUD workspace.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Best model not found. Did training complete successfully?\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
